# Per-instance state dirs are runtime (persistent-states/<INSTANCE>/) — keep
# only a README placeholder so the folder exists on a fresh clone. Default
# hooks/settings come from claude-sandbox-shared/, not from any instance dir.
persistent-states/*
!persistent-states/README.md

# Shared dir is also runtime, but track the default hooks scripts so a fresh
# clone has working hooks on first launch.
claude-sandbox-shared/*
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/
claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/*
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/hooks/
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/hooks/**
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/CLAUDE.md
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/settings.json
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/.caveman-active
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/PLUGIN_PINS.md
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/skills/
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/skills/**
# Vendor the caveman plugin source so a fresh clone has it without
# network round-trips to JuliusBrussee/caveman at first session. Pinned
# at v2.3.1 (commit b5ec6351...) — bump by replacing the tree in place
# and updating PLUGIN_PINS.md. The plugins/cache/ dir stays gitignored;
# claude-code rebuilds it from the vendored marketplaces tree on first
# session.
# Re-include the plugins tree, but ONLY the vendored marketplace sources.
# `!plugins/` alone lets git descend into plugins/, but the parent
# `.claude/*` rule is only one level deep so it never re-ignores the
# runtime children (cache/, installed_plugins.json, known_marketplaces.json,
# plugin-catalog-cache.json, .last_inuse_sweep, and runtime-cloned
# marketplaces like claude-plugins-official/). So blacklist everything
# under plugins/ and under marketplaces/, then whitelist just the two
# vendored trees. claude-code rebuilds cache/ and the runtime clones from
# these on first session.
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/
claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/*
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/
claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/*
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/caveman/
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/caveman/**
# Vendor ponytail same way — pinned at v4.9.0 (commit 0a4dd63a...).
# See PLUGIN_PINS.md for bump procedure.
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/ponytail/
!claude-sandbox-shared/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/ponytail/**


workspace/*
!workspace/README.md
set_working_dir.sh

# Ignore the contents of the context folder:
context_reference/*
!context_reference/README.md

SAVED_SNAPSHOTS

# Per-workspace env files (envs/env.<NAME>.sh) are user-specific. Only the
# template is tracked. Legacy root-level env.*.sh kept ignored for old clones.
envs/env.*.sh
!envs/env.example.sh
env.sh
env.*.sh
!env.example.sh

# Vertex-mode activation script holds a real GCP project id. Only the
# placeholder template is tracked.
SET_VERTEX_MODE.sh
!SET_VERTEX_MODE.example.sh

# Master workdir registry. Holds absolute host paths chosen by the user at
# launch time (union of env file candidates + every prior pick). Per-host
# state — regenerated by start_sandbox.sh on first run.
workdirs.txt

# Python bytecode cache. Leaks in when py_compile / pyflakes is run from
# the repo root against vertex_proxy.py.
__pycache__/

# Host-side fiss-mcp install artifacts. Only the install.sh + run-server.py
# tracked source files belong in git; the venv and cloned source tree are
# created fresh by setup_host.sh.
host_fiss_mcp/venv/
host_fiss_mcp/fiss-mcp/

# Session-history snapshots produced on demand by
# SESSION_ARCHIVE/archive_sessions.sh. The per-source subdirs hold
# hundreds of MB of session transcripts (full command + output history
# across all projects) — kept out of git for size and privacy. Only the
# script + README are tracked; re-run the script to regenerate the data.
SESSION_ARCHIVE/*/
# INDEX.md embeds first-prompt snippets from every project's sessions —
# regenerable via index_sessions.sh, kept out of git for the same
# size/privacy reasons as the archived data.
SESSION_ARCHIVE/INDEX.md
# CLASSIFIED.md embeds session titles + prompt snippets too — same
# privacy reason. It's your working attribution artifact, regenerable.
SESSION_ARCHIVE/CLASSIFIED.md

# Prewarmed HF model cache — downloaded by `make prewarm`, not source.
docker/hf-cache/

# Persistent shared HuggingFace cache for headroom (downloaded at runtime,
# not source). One copy shared by all instances.
hf-cache-runtime/

# Backups written by scripts/sync_env_template.py --go
envs/*.bak
